[2026-03-16T04:09:41.472Z] {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01KWBX78un6MDLFmyi97k13g","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! Now I have all the information I need. Let me compile a comprehensive report.\n\n## API Endpoints Usage Report\n\nI've thoroughly searched the codebase and found all the files that call these backend API endpoints. Here's the complete breakdown:\n\n---\n\n### 1. `/.netlify/functions/bookings` with `guest_id` param (My Trips)\n\n**File:** `/repo/apps/AirbnbClone/src/slices/bookingsSlice.ts`\n\n**Thunk Definition (Lines 59-69):**\n```typescript\nexport const fetchUserBookings = createAsyncThunk(\n  'bookings/fetchUserBookings',\n  async (guestId: string, { rejectWithValue }) => {\n    const response = await fetch(`/api/bookings?guest_id=${encodeURIComponent(guestId)}`)\n    const result = await response.json()\n    if (!response.ok) {\n      return rejectWithValue(result.error || 'Failed to fetch bookings')\n    }\n    return result as Booking[]\n  }\n)\n```\n\n**Response Type:** `Booking[]`\n- id, property_id, guest_id, check_in, check_out, num_guests, total_price, status\n- Additional fields: property_title, property_city, property_country, property_image, has_review\n\n**State Management (Lines 109-122):**\n```typescript\n.addCase(fetchUserBookings.pending, (state) => {\n  if (state.items.length === 0) {\n    state.loading = true\n  }\n  state.error = null\n})\n.addCase(fetchUserBookings.fulfilled, (state, action) => {\n  state.loading = false\n  state.items = action.payload  // Stored in state.bookings.items\n})\n.addCase(fetchUserBookings.rejected, (state, action) => {\n  state.loading = false\n  state.error = action.payload as string\n})\n```\n\n**Usage Pages:**\n- **MyTrips Page** (`/repo/apps/AirbnbClone/src/pages/MyTrips.tsx`, lines 5, 22):\n  - Dispatched in useEffect when currentUser is available\n  - Result stored in Redux and passed to TripsTabs component\n  - Used to display user's trips with ability to cancel bookings\n  \n```typescript\ndispatch(fetchUserBookings(currentUser.id))  // Line 22\nconst { items: bookings, loading } = useSelector((state: RootState) => state.bookings)\n```\n\n---\n\n### 2. `/.netlify/functions/reviews` with `property_id` or `guest_id` param\n\nThere are **two different uses of the reviews endpoint**:\n\n#### A. Fetching Reviews by Guest ID (User's Written Reviews)\n\n**File:** `/repo/apps/AirbnbClone/src/slices/userReviewsSlice.ts`\n\n**Thunk Definition (Lines 31-41):**\n```typescript\nexport const fetchUserReviews = createAsyncThunk(\n  'userReviews/fetchUserReviews',\n  async (guestId: string, { rejectWithValue }) => {\n    const response = await fetch(`/api/reviews?guest_id=${guestId}`)\n    const data = await response.json()\n    if (!response.ok) {\n      return rejectWithValue(data.error || 'Failed to fetch reviews')\n    }\n    return data as UserReview[]\n  }\n)\n```\n\n**Response Type:** `UserReview[]`\n- id, booking_id, property_id, guest_id, rating, cleanliness, accuracy, communication, location, value, comment, created_at, property_title\n\n**State Management (Lines 49-62):**\n```typescript\n.addCase(fetchUserReviews.pending, (state) => {\n  if (state.items.length === 0) {\n    state.loading = true\n  }\n  state.error = null\n})\n.addCase(fetchUserReviews.fulfilled, (state, action) => {\n  state.loading = false\n  state.items = action.payload  // Stored in state.userReviews.items\n})\n.addCase(fetchUserReviews.rejected, (state, action) => {\n  state.loading = false\n  state.error = action.payload as string\n})\n```\n\n**Usage Page:**\n- **Profile Page** (`/repo/apps/AirbnbClone/src/pages/Profile.tsx`, lines 5, 21):\n  - Dispatched in useEffect when currentUser is available\n  - Results displayed in UserReviewsList component\n  - Shows guest's written reviews with property link, rating, and comments\n\n```typescript\ndispatch(fetchUserReviews(currentUser.id))  // Line 21\nconst { items: reviews, loading: reviewsLoading } = useSelector((state: RootState) => state.userReviews)\n```\n\n#### B. Reviews Embedded in Property Detail Response\n\n**File:** `/repo/apps/AirbnbClone/src/slices/propertyDetailSlice.ts`\n\n**Thunk Definition (Lines 16-26):**\n```typescript\nexport const fetchPropertyDetail = createAsyncThunk(\n  'propertyDetail/fetchPropertyDetail',\n  async (propertyId: string, { rejectWithValue }) => {\n    const response = await fetch(`/api/properties/${propertyId}`)\n    const data = await response.json()\n    if (!response.ok) {\n      return rejectWithValue(data.error || 'Failed to fetch property')\n    }\n    return data as Property\n  }\n)\n```\n\n**Response Type:** `Property` (which includes `reviews?: Review[]`)\n\n**Review Type Definition** (`/repo/apps/AirbnbClone/src/slices/propertiesSlice.ts`, lines 18-33):\n```typescript\nexport interface Review {\n  id: string\n  booking_id: string\n  property_id: string\n  guest_id: string\n  rating: number\n  cleanliness: number\n  accuracy: number\n  communication: number\n  location: number\n  value: number\n  comment: string | null\n  created_at: string\n  guest_name: string\n  guest_avatar: string | null\n}\n```\n\n**Usage Page:**\n- **PropertyDetail Page** (`/repo/apps/AirbnbClone/src/pages/PropertyDetail.tsx`, lines 6, 24, 82):\n  - Dispatched in useEffect when propertyId param is available\n  - Reviews passed to ReviewsSection component\n\n```typescript\ndispatch(fetchPropertyDetail(id))  // Line 24\nconst { property, loading, error } = useSelector((state: RootState) => state.propertyDetail)\n<ReviewsSection reviews={property.reviews || []} />  // Line 82\n```\n\n**How Reviews Are Rendered** (`/repo/apps/AirbnbClone/src/components/ReviewsSection.tsx`):\n- Displays overall rating and review count (line 49)\n- Shows category averages: Cleanliness, Accuracy, Communication, Location, Value (lines 54-70)\n- Displays individual reviews in a grid with guest name, avatar, date, and comment (lines 74-107)\n- Initial show: 6 reviews, with \"Show all\" toggle (lines 9, 42, 110-118)\n\n---\n\n### 3. `/.netlify/functions/host-bookings` with `host_id` param\n\n**File:** `/repo/apps/AirbnbClone/src/slices/hostSlice.ts`\n\n**Thunk Definition (Lines 81-91):**\n```typescript\nexport const fetchHostBookings = createAsyncThunk(\n  'host/fetchHostBookings',\n  async (hostId: string, { rejectWithValue }) => {\n    const response = await fetch(`/api/host-bookings?host_id=${encodeURIComponent(hostId)}`)\n    const data = await response.json()\n    if (!response.ok) {\n      return rejectWithValue(data.error || 'Failed to fetch host bookings')\n    }\n    return data as HostBooking[]\n  }\n)\n```\n\n**Response Type:** `HostBooking[]`\n- Extends Booking with guest_name and guest_email\n\n**State Management (Lines 209-222):**\n```typescript\n.addCase(fetchHostBookings.pending, (state) => {\n  if (state.bookings.length === 0) {\n    state.bookingsLoading = true\n  }\n  state.error = null\n})\n.addCase(fetchHostBookings.fulfilled, (state, action) => {\n  state.bookingsLoading = false\n  state.bookings = action.payload  // Stored in state.host.bookings\n})\n.addCase(fetchHostBookings.rejected, (state, action) => {\n  state.bookingsLoading = false\n  state.error = action.payload as string\n})\n```\n\n**Usage Page:**\n- **HostDashboard Page** (`/repo/apps/AirbnbClone/src/pages/HostDashboard.tsx`, lines 7, 41, 154):\n  - Dispatched in useEffect when currentUser.is_host is true\n  - Results displayed in BookingsTab component with confirm/cancel actions\n\n```typescript\ndispatch(fetchHostBookings(currentUser.id))  // Line 41\nconst { bookings, bookingsLoading } = useSelector((state: RootState) => state.host)\n<BookingsTab bookings={bookings} loading={bookingsLoading} ... />  // Line 154\n```\n\n---\n\n### 4. `/.netlify/functions/host-listings` with `host_id` param\n\n**File:** `/repo/apps/AirbnbClone/src/slices/hostSlice.ts`\n\n**Thunk Definition (Lines 69-79):**\n```typescript\nexport const fetchHostListings = createAsyncThunk(\n  'host/fetchHostListings',\n  async (hostId: string, { rejectWithValue }) => {\n    const response = await fetch(`/api/host-listings?host_id=${encodeURIComponent(hostId)}`)\n    const data = await response.json()\n    if (!response.ok) {\n      return rejectWithValue(data.error || 'Failed to fetch host listings')\n    }\n    return data as Property[]\n  }\n)\n```\n\n**Response Type:** `Property[]`\n\n**State Management (Lines 195-208):**\n```typescript\n.addCase(fetchHostListings.pending, (state) => {\n  if (state.listings.length === 0) {\n    state.listingsLoading = true\n  }\n  state.error = null\n})\n.addCase(fetchHostListings.fulfilled, (state, action) => {\n  state.listingsLoading = false\n  state.listings = action.payload  // Stored in state.host.listings\n})\n.addCase(fetchHostListings.rejected, (state, action) => {\n  state.listingsLoading = false\n  state.error = action.payload as string\n})\n```\n\n**Usage Page:**\n- **HostDashboard Page** (`/repo/apps/AirbnbClone/src/pages/HostDashboard.tsx`, lines 7, 40, 142):\n  - Dispatched in useEffect when currentUser.is_host is true\n  - Results displayed in ListingsTab component with deactivate/activate actions\n\n```typescript\ndispatch(fetchHostListings(currentUser.id))  // Line 40\nconst { listings, listingsLoading } = useSelector((state: RootState) => state.host)\n<ListingsTab listings={listings} loading={listingsLoading} ... />  // Line 142\n```\n\n---\n\n### 5. `/.netlify/functions/favorites` with `user_id` param\n\n**File:** `/repo/apps/AirbnbClone/src/slices/favoritesSlice.ts`\n\n**Thunk Definition (Lines 13-23):**\n```typescript\nexport const fetchFavorites = createAsyncThunk(\n  'favorites/fetchFavorites',\n  async (userId: string, { rejectWithValue }) => {\n    const response = await fetch(`/api/favorites?user_id=${userId}`)\n    const data = await response.json()\n    if (!response.ok) {\n      return rejectWithValue(data.error || 'Failed to fetch favorites')\n    }\n    return (data as { property_id: string }[]).map((f) => f.property_id)\n  }\n)\n```\n\n**Response Type:** `string[]` (array of property IDs)\n\n**State Management (Lines 61-70):**\n```typescript\n.addCase(fetchFavorites.pending, (state) => {\n  state.loading = true\n})\n.addCase(fetchFavorites.fulfilled, (state, action) => {\n  state.loading = false\n  state.propertyIds = action.payload  // Stored in state.favorites.propertyIds as array\n})\n.addCase(fetchFavorites.rejected, (state) => {\n  state.loading = false\n})\n```\n\n**Usage Page:**\n- **Home Page** (`/repo/apps/AirbnbClone/src/pages/Home.tsx`, lines 5, 23):\n  - Dispatched in useEffect when currentUser is available\n  - Used by FavoriteButton component to determine heart icon fill state\n\n```typescript\ndispatch(fetchFavorites(currentUser.id))  // Line 23\nconst favoriteIds = useSelector((state: RootState) => state.favorites.propertyIds)\n```\n\n**Usage Component:**\n- **FavoriteButton** (`/repo/apps/AirbnbClone/src/components/FavoriteButton.tsx`, lines 4, 13):\n  - Checks if property is in favoriteIds array (line 14)\n  - Dispatches addFavorite or removeFavorite on click (lines 22-25)\n\n```typescript\nconst isFavorited = favoriteIds.includes(propertyId)\n```\n\n---\n\n## Summary Table\n\n| Endpoint | Parameter | Response Type | Used By | Storage |\n|----------|-----------|--------------|---------|---------|\n| `/api/bookings` | `guest_id` | `Booking[]` | MyTrips page | `state.bookings.items` |\n| `/api/reviews` | `guest_id` | `UserReview[]` | Profile page | `state.userReviews.items` |\n| `/api/properties/{id}` | (path param) | `Property` (includes `reviews[]`) | PropertyDetail page | `state.propertyDetail.property` |\n| `/api/host-bookings` | `host_id` | `HostBooking[]` | HostDashboard page | `state.host.bookings` |\n| `/api/host-listings` | `host_id` | `Property[]` | HostDashboard page | `state.host.listings` |\n| `/api/favorites` | `user_id` | `{property_id}[]` → `string[]` | Home page | `state.favorites.propertyIds` |\n\nAll API calls use Redux async thunks with proper error handling, loading states, and response transformation before storage in Redux state."},{"type":"text","text":"agentId: a24304f7c8904a54a (for resuming to continue this agent's work if needed)\n<usage>total_tokens: 49606\ntool_uses: 24\nduration_ms: 40476</usage>"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4877f3d7-4b15-4027-8594-e225d536fda7","uuid":"8a97bec2-c8ec-4b77-99c4-1b11cd577943","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"In /repo/apps/AirbnbClone/src, find all files that call these backend API endpoints and show me how they consume the responses. I need to understand how these are used:\n\n1. `/.netlify/functions/bookings` with `guest_id` param (My Trips)\n2. `/.netlify/functions/reviews` with `property_id` or `guest_id` param\n3. `/.netlify/functions/host-bookings` with `host_id` param\n4. `/.netlify/functions/host-listings` with `host_id` param\n5. `/.netlify/functions/favorites` with `user_id` param\n\nAlso look at the property detail page - specifically how reviews are rendered from the properties endpoint response (reviews embedded in property detail).\n\nSearch for fetch calls, API utility functions, Redux thunks, or any abstraction layer that makes these API calls. Show me the relevant code snippets with file paths and line numbers. Be thorough - check for patterns like \"host-bookings\", \"host-listings\", \"bookings?guest_id\", \"reviews?property_id\", etc.","agentId":"a24304f7c8904a54a","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! Now I have all the information I need. Let me compile a comprehensive report.\n\n## API Endpoints Usage Report\n\nI've thoroughly searched the codebase and found all the files that call these backend API endpoints. Here's the complete breakdown:\n\n---\n\n### 1. `/.netlify/functions/bookings` with `guest_id` param (My Trips)\n\n**File:** `/repo/apps/AirbnbClone/src/slices/bookingsSlice.ts`\n\n**Thunk Definition (Lines 59-69):**\n```typescript\nexport const fetchUserBookings = createAsyncThunk(\n  'bookings/fetchUserBookings',\n  async (guestId: string, { rejectWithValue }) => {\n    const response = await fetch(`/api/bookings?guest_id=${encodeURIComponent(guestId)}`)\n    const result = await response.json()\n    if (!response.ok) {\n      return rejectWithValue(result.error || 'Failed to fetch bookings')\n    }\n    return result as Booking[]\n  }\n)\n```\n\n**Response Type:** `Booking[]`\n- id, property_id, guest_id, check_in, check_out, num_guests, total_price, status\n- Additional fields: property_title, property_city, property_country, property_image, has_review\n\n**State Management (Lines 109-122):**\n```typescript\n.addCase(fetchUserBookings.pending, (state) => {\n  if (state.items.length === 0) {\n    state.loading = true\n  }\n  state.error = null\n})\n.addCase(fetchUserBookings.fulfilled, (state, action) => {\n  state.loading = false\n  state.items = action.payload  // Stored in state.bookings.items\n})\n.addCase(fetchUserBookings.rejected, (state, action) => {\n  state.loading = false\n  state.error = action.payload as string\n})\n```\n\n**Usage Pages:**\n- **MyTrips Page** (`/repo/apps/AirbnbClone/src/pages/MyTrips.tsx`, lines 5, 22):\n  - Dispatched in useEffect when currentUser is available\n  - Result stored in Redux and passed to TripsTabs component\n  - Used to display user's trips with ability to cancel bookings\n  \n```typescript\ndispatch(fetchUserBookings(currentUser.id))  // Line 22\nconst { items: bookings, loading } = useSelector((state: RootState) => state.bookings)\n```\n\n---\n\n### 2. `/.netlify/functions/reviews` with `property_id` or `guest_id` param\n\nThere are **two different uses of the reviews endpoint**:\n\n#### A. Fetching Reviews by Guest ID (User's Written Reviews)\n\n**File:** `/repo/apps/AirbnbClone/src/slices/userReviewsSlice.ts`\n\n**Thunk Definition (Lines 31-41):**\n```typescript\nexport const fetchUserReviews = createAsyncThunk(\n  'userReviews/fetchUserReviews',\n  async (guestId: string, { rejectWithValue }) => {\n    const response = await fetch(`/api/reviews?guest_id=${guestId}`)\n    const data = await response.json()\n    if (!response.ok) {\n      return rejectWithValue(data.error || 'Failed to fetch reviews')\n    }\n    return data as UserReview[]\n  }\n)\n```\n\n**Response Type:** `UserReview[]`\n- id, booking_id, property_id, guest_id, rating, cleanliness, accuracy, communication, location, value, comment, created_at, property_title\n\n**State Management (Lines 49-62):**\n```typescript\n.addCase(fetchUserReviews.pending, (state) => {\n  if (state.items.length === 0) {\n    state.loading = true\n  }\n  state.error = null\n})\n.addCase(fetchUserReviews.fulfilled, (state, action) => {\n  state.loading = false\n  state.items = action.payload  // Stored in state.userReviews.items\n})\n.addCase(fetchUserReviews.rejected, (state, action) => {\n  state.loading = false\n  state.error = action.payload as string\n})\n```\n\n**Usage Page:**\n- **Profile Page** (`/repo/apps/AirbnbClone/src/pages/Profile.tsx`, lines 5, 21):\n  - Dispatched in useEffect when currentUser is available\n  - Results displayed in UserReviewsList component\n  - Shows guest's written reviews with property link, rating, and comments\n\n```typescript\ndispatch(fetchUserReviews(currentUser.id))  // Line 21\nconst { items: reviews, loading: reviewsLoading } = useSelector((state: RootState) => state.userReviews)\n```\n\n#### B. Reviews Embedded in Property Detail Response\n\n**File:** `/repo/apps/AirbnbClone/src/slices/propertyDetailSlice.ts`\n\n**Thunk Definition (Lines 16-26):**\n```typescript\nexport const fetchPropertyDetail = createAsyncThunk(\n  'propertyDetail/fetchPropertyDetail',\n  async (propertyId: string, { rejectWithValue }) => {\n    const response = await fetch(`/api/properties/${propertyId}`)\n    const data = await response.json()\n    if (!response.ok) {\n      return rejectWithValue(data.error || 'Failed to fetch property')\n    }\n    return data as Property\n  }\n)\n```\n\n**Response Type:** `Property` (which includes `reviews?: Review[]`)\n\n**Review Type Definition** (`/repo/apps/AirbnbClone/src/slices/propertiesSlice.ts`, lines 18-33):\n```typescript\nexport interface Review {\n  id: string\n  booking_id: string\n  property_id: string\n  guest_id: string\n  rating: number\n  cleanliness: number\n  accuracy: number\n  communication: number\n  location: number\n  value: number\n  comment: string | null\n  created_at: string\n  guest_name: string\n  guest_avatar: string | null\n}\n```\n\n**Usage Page:**\n- **PropertyDetail Page** (`/repo/apps/AirbnbClone/src/pages/PropertyDetail.tsx`, lines 6, 24, 82):\n  - Dispatched in useEffect when propertyId param is available\n  - Reviews passed to ReviewsSection component\n\n```typescript\ndispatch(fetchPropertyDetail(id))  // Line 24\nconst { property, loading, error } = useSelector((state: RootState) => state.propertyDetail)\n<ReviewsSection reviews={property.reviews || []} />  // Line 82\n```\n\n**How Reviews Are Rendered** (`/repo/apps/AirbnbClone/src/components/ReviewsSection.tsx`):\n- Displays overall rating and review count (line 49)\n- Shows category averages: Cleanliness, Accuracy, Communication, Location, Value (lines 54-70)\n- Displays individual reviews in a grid with guest name, avatar, date, and comment (lines 74-107)\n- Initial show: 6 reviews, with \"Show all\" toggle (lines 9, 42, 110-118)\n\n---\n\n### 3. `/.netlify/functions/host-bookings` with `host_id` param\n\n**File:** `/repo/apps/AirbnbClone/src/slices/hostSlice.ts`\n\n**Thunk Definition (Lines 81-91):**\n```typescript\nexport const fetchHostBookings = createAsyncThunk(\n  'host/fetchHostBookings',\n  async (hostId: string, { rejectWithValue }) => {\n    const response = await fetch(`/api/host-bookings?host_id=${encodeURIComponent(hostId)}`)\n    const data = await response.json()\n    if (!response.ok) {\n      return rejectWithValue(data.error || 'Failed to fetch host bookings')\n    }\n    return data as HostBooking[]\n  }\n)\n```\n\n**Response Type:** `HostBooking[]`\n- Extends Booking with guest_name and guest_email\n\n**State Management (Lines 209-222):**\n```typescript\n.addCase(fetchHostBookings.pending, (state) => {\n  if (state.bookings.length === 0) {\n    state.bookingsLoading = true\n  }\n  state.error = null\n})\n.addCase(fetchHostBookings.fulfilled, (state, action) => {\n  state.bookingsLoading = false\n  state.bookings = action.payload  // Stored in state.host.bookings\n})\n.addCase(fetchHostBookings.rejected, (state, action) => {\n  state.bookingsLoading = false\n  state.error = action.payload as string\n})\n```\n\n**Usage Page:**\n- **HostDashboard Page** (`/repo/apps/AirbnbClone/src/pages/HostDashboard.tsx`, lines 7, 41, 154):\n  - Dispatched in useEffect when currentUser.is_host is true\n  - Results displayed in BookingsTab component with confirm/cancel actions\n\n```typescript\ndispatch(fetchHostBookings(currentUser.id))  // Line 41\nconst { bookings, bookingsLoading } = useSelector((state: RootState) => state.host)\n<BookingsTab bookings={bookings} loading={bookingsLoading} ... />  // Line 154\n```\n\n---\n\n### 4. `/.netlify/functions/host-listings` with `host_id` param\n\n**File:** `/repo/apps/AirbnbClone/src/slices/hostSlice.ts`\n\n**Thunk Definition (Lines 69-79):**\n```typescript\nexport const fetchHostListings = createAsyncThunk(\n  'host/fetchHostListings',\n  async (hostId: string, { rejectWithValue }) => {\n    const response = await fetch(`/api/host-listings?host_id=${encodeURIComponent(hostId)}`)\n    const data = await response.json()\n    if (!response.ok) {\n      return rejectWithValue(data.error || 'Failed to fetch host listings')\n    }\n    return data as Property[]\n  }\n)\n```\n\n**Response Type:** `Property[]`\n\n**State Management (Lines 195-208):**\n```typescript\n.addCase(fetchHostListings.pending, (state) => {\n  if (state.listings.length === 0) {\n    state.listingsLoading = true\n  }\n  state.error = null\n})\n.addCase(fetchHostListings.fulfilled, (state, action) => {\n  state.listingsLoading = false\n  state.listings = action.payload  // Stored in state.host.listings\n})\n.addCase(fetchHostListings.rejected, (state, action) => {\n  state.listingsLoading = false\n  state.error = action.payload as string\n})\n```\n\n**Usage Page:**\n- **HostDashboard Page** (`/repo/apps/AirbnbClone/src/pages/HostDashboard.tsx`, lines 7, 40, 142):\n  - Dispatched in useEffect when currentUser.is_host is true\n  - Results displayed in ListingsTab component with deactivate/activate actions\n\n```typescript\ndispatch(fetchHostListings(currentUser.id))  // Line 40\nconst { listings, listingsLoading } = useSelector((state: RootState) => state.host)\n<ListingsTab listings={listings} loading={listingsLoading} ... />  // Line 142\n```\n\n---\n\n### 5. `/.netlify/functions/favorites` with `user_id` param\n\n**File:** `/repo/apps/AirbnbClone/src/slices/favoritesSlice.ts`\n\n**Thunk Definition (Lines 13-23):**\n```typescript\nexport const fetchFavorites = createAsyncThunk(\n  'favorites/fetchFavorites',\n  async (userId: string, { rejectWithValue }) => {\n    const response = await fetch(`/api/favorites?user_id=${userId}`)\n    const data = await response.json()\n    if (!response.ok) {\n      return rejectWithValue(data.error || 'Failed to fetch favorites')\n    }\n    return (data as { property_id: string }[]).map((f) => f.property_id)\n  }\n)\n```\n\n**Response Type:** `string[]` (array of property IDs)\n\n**State Management (Lines 61-70):**\n```typescript\n.addCase(fetchFavorites.pending, (state) => {\n  state.loading = true\n})\n.addCase(fetchFavorites.fulfilled, (state, action) => {\n  state.loading = false\n  state.propertyIds = action.payload  // Stored in state.favorites.propertyIds as array\n})\n.addCase(fetchFavorites.rejected, (state) => {\n  state.loading = false\n})\n```\n\n**Usage Page:**\n- **Home Page** (`/repo/apps/AirbnbClone/src/pages/Home.tsx`, lines 5, 23):\n  - Dispatched in useEffect when currentUser is available\n  - Used by FavoriteButton component to determine heart icon fill state\n\n```typescript\ndispatch(fetchFavorites(currentUser.id))  // Line 23\nconst favoriteIds = useSelector((state: RootState) => state.favorites.propertyIds)\n```\n\n**Usage Component:**\n- **FavoriteButton** (`/repo/apps/AirbnbClone/src/components/FavoriteButton.tsx`, lines 4, 13):\n  - Checks if property is in favoriteIds array (line 14)\n  - Dispatches addFavorite or removeFavorite on click (lines 22-25)\n\n```typescript\nconst isFavorited = favoriteIds.includes(propertyId)\n```\n\n---\n\n## Summary Table\n\n| Endpoint | Parameter | Response Type | Used By | Storage |\n|----------|-----------|--------------|---------|---------|\n| `/api/bookings` | `guest_id` | `Booking[]` | MyTrips page | `state.bookings.items` |\n| `/api/reviews` | `guest_id` | `UserReview[]` | Profile page | `state.userReviews.items` |\n| `/api/properties/{id}` | (path param) | `Property` (includes `reviews[]`) | PropertyDetail page | `state.propertyDetail.property` |\n| `/api/host-bookings` | `host_id` | `HostBooking[]` | HostDashboard page | `state.host.bookings` |\n| `/api/host-listings` | `host_id` | `Property[]` | HostDashboard page | `state.host.listings` |\n| `/api/favorites` | `user_id` | `{property_id}[]` → `string[]` | Home page | `state.favorites.propertyIds` |\n\nAll API calls use Redux async thunks with proper error handling, loading states, and response transformation before storage in Redux state."}],"totalDurationMs":40476,"totalTokens":49606,"totalToolUseCount":24,"usage":{"input_tokens":5,"cache_creation_input_tokens":431,"cache_read_input_tokens":45468,"output_tokens":3702,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":431},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"}}}
